<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samerina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from c. 720 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samerina was the Assyrian province created from the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a> in 722–720 BCE, with Samaria as its seat. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> deported part of the population and settled people from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and elsewhere in their place. The province later passed under Babylonian and then Persian rule, when it was known as Samaria.</p></div>
